STEP 1: Write a pod by hand (no copy-paste!)
--------------------------------------------
vi pod-web.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: web
  labels:
    app: web
    tier: frontend
spec:
  containers:
  - name: web
    image: nginx:1.27
    ports:
    - containerPort: 80

Validate, then apply:
  k apply -f pod-web.yaml --dry-run=client
  k apply -f pod-web.yaml
  k get pods --show-labels


STEP 2: Break the YAML on purpose
---------------------------------
a) Replace the 2 spaces before "- name: web" with a TAB and apply.
   Read the error. Fix it.
b) Change "containers" to "container". Apply. Read the error
   ("unknown field"). Fix it.
c) Change "kind: Pod" to "kind: pod". What happens?

Lesson: the error message tells you the line or field. Read it.


STEP 3: Generate YAML
---------------------
k run gen --image=nginx:1.27 --port=80 --labels=app=gen --dry-run=client -o yaml > pod-gen.yaml
cat pod-gen.yaml

Notice the extra fields (creationTimestamp: null, resources: {},
status: {}). They are harmless; delete them to keep files clean.

k apply -f pod-gen.yaml


STEP 4: Use k explain like a manual
-----------------------------------
k explain pod
k explain pod.spec
k explain pod.spec.containers
k explain pod.spec.containers.env
k explain pod.spec.restartPolicy

Answer from the output: what are the allowed values of restartPolicy,
and what is the default?


STEP 5: Update a pod with apply (and hit the immutability wall)
---------------------------------------------------------------
Edit pod-web.yaml: add a label "version: v1" under labels. Apply.
  k apply -f pod-web.yaml
  k get pod web --show-labels           # label changed in place: OK

Now change the image to nginx:1.26 and apply. This works (image is
one of the few mutable fields). Watch the RESTARTS column:
  k get pod web

Now add a second port (containerPort: 8080) and apply.
  -> Error: "Pod updates may not change fields other than ..."
Pods are mostly immutable. Fix with:
  k delete -f pod-web.yaml && k apply -f pod-web.yaml
or:
  k replace --force -f pod-web.yaml


STEP 6: k diff
--------------
Change the label tier: frontend to tier: web in pod-web.yaml.
  k diff -f pod-web.yaml
Read the diff, then apply.


STEP 7: Several objects in one file
-----------------------------------
vi two-pods.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: one
spec:
  containers:
  - name: c
    image: busybox:1.36
    command: ["sh", "-c", "sleep 3600"]
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: two
spec:
  containers:
  - name: c
    image: busybox:1.36
    command: ["sh", "-c", "sleep 3600"]

k apply -f two-pods.yaml
k get pods
k delete -f two-pods.yaml


STEP 8: Apply a whole folder
----------------------------
k apply -f .          # applies every YAML in the folder
k get pods
k delete -f .         # deletes everything the folder describes


